  "result": "Excellent! All 98 tests pass. I've successfully added customer tier-based discounts:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **src/customers.js** \u2014 Added `TIER_DISCOUNTS` export:\n   ```javascript\n   export const TIER_DISCOUNTS = {\n     gold: 5,\n     silver: 2.5,\n     standard: 0,\n   };\n   ```\n\n2. **src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated `createInvoice` and `addLine` to apply tier discounts:\n   - When a line has no `discountPercent` in the input, the customer's tier discount is automatically applied\n   - An explicit `discountPercent` (even 0) always overrides the tier discount\n   - The final discount is validated before use\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 11 new tier-discount tests covering:\n   - Gold customers get 5% by default\n   - Silver customers get 2.5% by default  \n   - Standard customers get 0% by default\n   - Explicit discounts override tier discounts\n   - Explicit 0 overrides tier discounts\n   - Multiple lines each get the tier discount\n   - addLine behavior with tier discounts\n   - invoiceTotals respects tier discounts\n\nAll existing tests were updated to account for tier discounts being applied by default based on customer tier. The system now centrally manages tier discount percentages in one place, making them easy to update if needed.\n\nReady for the next request.",
